- Only 56% of households earning less than $30,000 per year have access to broadband internet, compared to 93% of households earning $75,000 or more.
- Black and Hispanic adults are less likely to have access to home broadband than White adults.
- Older adults (ages 65 and older) are less likely to have access to home broadband than younger adults.
To bridge the digital divide, multifaceted strategies have been proposed and implemented. Some of these strategies include:
- Expanding broadband infrastructure in underserved areas
- Providing affordable internet and technology options to low-income households
- Increasing digital literacy and technology training programs
- Encouraging private sector investment in underserved areas
