How can we implement a binary search algorithm in C++ while also adhering to formal and professional writing standards? And can you explain how this algorithm can be used to efficiently search for a particular value in a sorted array?
Here's an example implementation of a binary search algorithm in C++:
```c++
int binarySearch(int arr[], int l, int r, int x) {
    if (r >= l) {
        int mid = l + (r - l) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] == x) {
            return mid;
        }
        if (arr[mid] > x) {
            return binarySearch(arr, l, mid - 1, x);
        }
        return binarySearch(arr, mid + 1, r, x);
    }
    return -1;
}
```
To use this algorithm, you simply call the `binarySearch` function with the array to search, the left and right indices of the subarray to search, and the value you're looking for. The function returns the index of the value if it's found, or `-1` if it's not present in the array.
Remember to use clear and descriptive variable names, and to properly comment your code to make it easier to understand and maintain.

